      "message": "Okay I will change the comment style.\n\nYes we don\u0027t have a way to find out anti-collapse for BC1.2 chargers (weak or slow chargers).\n\nYes we don\u0027t check anti-collapse status anywhere.\n\nI have a plan to create another CL: For non-BC1.2 compliant chargers we can set current limit as 2.4A (2.4A apple charger).\nAfter setting the IBUS_LIM_SET \u0026 ICC_LIM_SET (at board level set event for USB charger task) we can check for the CUR_ILIM_VAL. \nIF CUR_ILIM_VAL has dropped by 1/2 or 1/4 or to 128mA (configurable in CHGOP_SET2) we can consider it as anti-collapse.\nWe can keep lowering the IBUS_LIM_SET \u0026 ICC_LIM_SET (2A, 1.5A, 1A, 500mA) until we get same CUR_ILIM_VAL and then update the charge manger with new values.",
